		{
			"id": "euiNbCZxLP28RiOD0",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark II (Heretic)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRequires the black carapace interface to move and fight at full efficiency. Early plate with poor seals even when new, and no forge-temple has serviced this one in ten thousand years (Weak Points 7). Rigid heavy armour DX/Stealth penalties apply.\n\nLore: Mark II plate was worn by the Legions of the Great Crusade, so a great deal of it ended up on the traitor side of the Horus Heresy. Warbands still wear it, patched with spikes, cast-off trophies and whatever their own armourers can bang into shape. Black Library Horus Heresy and Chaos Space Marine fiction shows traitor plate as worn, scarred and repaired in the field.\n\nDesign: DR, servo ST, weight and cost are those of the loyalist Mark II (Crusade Pattern) entry, which this entry includes. Weak Points are one higher, 6 to 7, as the Chaos section of framework.md directs: ten thousand years without a forge-temple means worn seals and hand-mended joints, though the plate itself is as thick as ever.",
