		{
			"id": "ehh_8L4cauyukFENP",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark III (Heretic)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nHeaviest of the Heresy-era patterns (treat as an extra -1 to Dodge or an extra step of encumbrance at the GM's discretion, on top of the usual rigid heavy armour penalties). Requires the black carapace interface. Worn seals and joints: Weak Points 5.\n\nLore: Iron Armour was the plate of breaching and siege work in the Heresy and is still worn by traitor assault troops, its thick frontal plate now dented, rewelded and often marked with the sigils of a god. The Chaos forges that keep it running do so by habit and sorcery, not by the rites of the Cult Mechanicus.\n\nDesign: DR, servo ST, weight and cost are those of the loyalist Mark III entry, included unchanged. Weak Points go from 4 to 5 (framework.md, Chaos: armour keeps the loyalist DR of its mark with Weak Points +1).",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Chaos",
				"Heretic Astartes"
			],
