		{
			"id": "e2AllwgV5gjX70NrO",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark VI (Heretic)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nReduced bulk penalty (as Mark IV) reflecting the pattern's emphasis on speed. Requires the black carapace interface. Worn seals and joints: Weak Points 6.\n\nLore: The light Corvus pattern went to the Legions that favoured speed and ambush, and a share of those Legions turned traitor. Their surviving suits keep the beaked helm and the light frame, and the long-unserviced joints that go with them.\n\nDesign: DR, servo ST, weight and cost match the loyalist Mark VI entry, included unchanged. Weak Points 5 to 6 as for every traitor suit (framework.md, Chaos).",
