		{
			"id": "EK-_5YN0IHjDzS0TK",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark VII (Heretic)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nSame suit as the loyalist Mark VII (Aquila Pattern) with worn seals and joints, Weak Points 5 rather than 4. Requires the black carapace interface: without one the wearer fights at -4 DX and half Basic Move and cannot use the auto-senses or weapon interlocks. Assembled weight 240 lb; the subsystems below are part of the suit, not extras.\n\nLore: Mark VII plate is mostly a loyalist pattern, but renegade Chapters and Legionaries who looted a loyalist armoury wear it too. In Chaos hands the suit is rarely maintained to the standard a Chapter armoury would keep.\n\nDesign: Included from the loyalist Mark VII entry, so the DR, weight (150 lb shell, 240 lb with subsystems), cost, and the subsystem children (auto-senses, vox, respirator, recyclers, servo actuators with lifting 9 and striking 5 ST on the servo child only) are identical. The only change is Weak Points 4 to 5 (framework.md, Chaos).",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Chaos",
				"Heretic Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "40000",
			"base_weight": "150 lb",
			"features": [
				{
