		{
			"id": "eFRWJN5Llrlv36x0Q",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark IV (Rubric)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nSealed. The suit's seals are soldered shut and the wearer is dust, so there is no flesh behind a gap in the plate. Weak Points are the loyalist figure, 5. Normally worn by a Rubric Marine; the servo ST listed still applies.\n\nLore: After the Rubric of Ahriman, the Thousand Sons who survived as dust were sealed into their armour. The suit is closed with sorcerous seals and kept in repair by the Legion's sorcerers, so it is in better condition than most traitor plate (Black Library, the Horus Heresy novel A Thousand Sons, and later Thousand Sons fiction).\n\nDesign: Mark IV DR, servo ST, weight and cost as the loyalist entry, included unchanged. Weak Points stay at the loyalist 5 rather than the heretic 6: the framework (Chaos, armour) says Rubric plate has the seals soldered shut, so the one thing that wears in other traitor suits has been fixed. Nothing inside to wound through a gap is covered by the Rubric Marine's own traits, not by this entry.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Chaos",
				"Heretic Astartes",
				"Tzeentch",
				"Thousand Sons"
			],
